---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { buyingFaqs } from '../lib/programs'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Programs FAQ"
  description="Frequently asked questions for institutions evaluating Castalia programs."
>
  <main class="programs-page section">
    <div class="section__intro">
      <h1>FAQ</h1>
      <p>
        Common questions from institutional buyers, program directors, and implementation teams.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-cards">
      {buyingFaqs.map((item) => (
        <article class="card">
          <h2>{item.question}</h2>
          <p>{item.answer}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Do programs require a specific LMS?</h2>
        <p>
          No single LMS is required. Offerings can be packaged for common LMS environments or
          delivered through supported hosted workflows depending on the program.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Can we start with a narrow audience?</h2>
        <p>
          Yes. Many partners begin with a special topics section, honors cohort, summer pilot, or
          executive education audience before scaling wider.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h2>What does implementation support include?</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on scope, support can include faculty onboarding, launch planning, learner
          communications, delivery recommendations, and reporting structure.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
